{"name":"Barren","hex":"#b9aba3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barren","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not bearing children, childless; hence also unable to bear children, sterile.","Not bearing seed or fruit."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of low fertility and habitation, a desolate place.","In particular, a usually elevated and flat expanse of land that only supports the growth of small trees and shrubs, and sometimes mosses or heathers, berries, and other marshy or moory vegetation, but little agriculture and few people."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barren"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barren, Missouri","blocks":[{"text":"Barren is an extinct town in southern Carter County, in the Ozarks of southeastern Missouri, United States. The community was located on the banks of Big Barren Creek, just north of the Carter - Ripley county line. The area is within the Mark Twain National Forest."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barren%2C_Missouri","wikidata":"Q27995136"},{"title":"Barren County, Kentucky","blocks":[{"text":"Barren County is a county located in the south-central portion of the U.S. state of Kentucky. As of the 2020 census, the population was 44,485. Its county seat is Glasgow. The county was founded on December 20, 1798, from parts of Warren and Green Counties. It was named for the Barrens, meadowlands that cover the northern third, though actually the soil is fertile. Barren County is part of the Glasgow, KY Micropolitan Statistical Area, which is also included in the Bowling Green-Glasgow, KY Combined Statistical Area. In 2007 Barren County was named the \"Best Place to Live in Rural America\" by Progressive Farmer Magazine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Barren_County_Kentucky_courthouse_2.jpg/330px-Barren_County_Kentucky_courthouse_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barren_County%2C_Kentucky","wikidata":"Q486081"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Kelly_Knight_Craft.jpg/500px-Kelly_Knight_Craft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Kelly_Knight_Craft.jpg/1280px-Kelly_Knight_Craft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Kelly_Knight_Craft.jpg/500px-Kelly_Knight_Craft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kelly Craft","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKelly_Knight_Craft.jpg"}],"sounds":{"barren":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/En-us-barren.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/97/En-us-barren.ogg/En-us-barren.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey bucchero-ware bowl, Clay, 1000-700 BCE, Nr. Babakõy, Turkey, Fitzwilliam Museum, Cambridge","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg/500px-Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg","ratio":0.8,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl,_Clay,_1000-700_BCE,_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y,_Turkey,_Fitzwilliam_Museum,_Cambridge.jpg","share":0.646875},{"title":"Cape Barren goose (Cereopsis novaehollandiae) pair with juvenile Maria Island","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Cape_Barren_goose_%28Cereopsis_novaehollandiae%29_pair_with_juvenile_Maria_Island.jpg/500px-Cape_Barren_goose_%28Cereopsis_novaehollandiae%29_pair_with_juvenile_Maria_Island.jpg",